+Road+Boca+Raton+FL+33498","access_notes":"The admission-free boardwalk is open sunrise–sunset. Pets, food, alcohol, running, biking, skating, smoking, and fishing are prohibited.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"pondhawk-natural-area","subject_type":"activity","entity_name":"Pondhawk Natural Area","title":"Loop Pondhawk’s Trails","subtitle":"Beside Spanish River Library · 1501 Spanish River Boulevard","notes":"Enter through the library parking lot, choose a marked trail, and regroup at the covered wetland observation platform.","short_summary":"Walk or bike around Blue Lake and restored wetlands at a public natural area.","evidence_claim":"Palm Beach County identifies Pondhawk as a public-use natural area, and its natural-areas guidance says these lands are free for passive activities including hiking and birdwatching.","source_url":"https://discover.pbcgov.org/erm/NaturalAreas/Pondhawk.aspx","source_title":"Environmental Resources Management - Pondhawk","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Pondhawk+Natural+Area+1501+Spanish+River+Boulevard+Boca+Raton+FL","access_notes":"Open sunrise–sunset every day. Enter via the Spanish River Library lot; natural-area rules prohibit pets, drones, and alcohol.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"boca-aquarium","subject_type":"place","entity_name":"Boca Aquarium","title":"Meet at the Boca Aquarium","subtitle":"2801 North Federal Highway · Boca Raton","notes":"Stop in during posted hours to see the shark, reef, nano-reef, and seahorse tanks; Thursday afternoons include shark feeding.","short_summary":"Take a compact, admission-free aquarium break a short drive from campus.","evidence_claim":"Boca Aquarium’s official visitor page states that admission is always free and lists its tanks, hours, address, and Thursday shark feeding.","source_url":"h